model lh16light
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "Cooley, Hubbard and Walz (1999), the Trinity study update. A portfolio of $1,000 is rebalanced every month to a stock/bond mix (Tables 1-4) or to 60% stock, 30% bonds and 10% Treasury bills (Tables 5-6). It earns each month's return and pays rate/12 of the initial value at the end of the month. The payment is fixed in dollars (Equation 1) or scaled each year by CPI(Y-1) / CPI(1925) (Equation 2). The periods are 15 to 30 years, from January 1926 or January 1946, through December 1997. No taxes, fees or transaction costs are modelled; the article mentions none."
  note "Cohort c starts with v0 at the start of month c. Iterating Equation (1) or (2) over months k = 1..T gives V_T = G_T x (v0 - v0 x rate/12 x the sum over k of scale_k / G_k), where G_k is the growth through month k. disc is 1 / G, and the terminal value is written in that closed form. The monthly portfolio return is the mix-weighted sum of the asset returns (monthly rebalancing, Methodology, PDF p. 3)."
  note "The data is Ibbotson SBBI 1998, a commercial product the case does not hold. The return and CPI inputs have no rows, so every success rate and every Table 6 statistic is a hole until a version supplies them."
  note "Light cut of models/LH-16.tally (regress/light). Only sizes change: the payout periods are 1 to 4 years instead of 15 to 30 (version light_sizes), so step runs 0..48; the success-rate asks keep six of the sixty table rows, Table 6 keeps panel A and the text reading; every ask pins one combination of the axes its cone reaches. Every section, rule, built-in and axis of LH-16 stays."

source lifted_1_0_1 "Figures tally 1.0.1 allowed inline in rules"

source light_cut "The light cut-down's own sizes (regress/light/LH-16-light.md): not a source's figures"

source trinity99 "Cooley, Hubbard, Walz, Sustainable Withdrawal Rates From Your Retirement Portfolio, Financial Counseling and Planning 10(1), 1999, pp. 41-51 (PDF mirror)" at "https://everywhereonce.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/10/trinity-study1.pdf"

unit USD: currency minor 0.01

axis cpi_base
  y1925 "Equation (2) as printed: every cohort's withdrawals are scaled by CPI(Y-1) / CPI(1925)"
  rebased "the base is the CPI of the year before the cohort's start year, so each cohort's first-year withdrawal is rate/12 of $1,000"

axis cpi_value
  annual_avg "CPI(Y) is the annual average CPI-U of year Y"
  december "CPI(Y) is the December CPI-U of year Y"

axis pct_round
  down "success rates truncated to the whole percent"
  half-even "success rates to the nearest whole percent, ties to even"
  half-up "success rates to the nearest whole percent, ties up"
  up "success rates rounded up to the whole percent"

axis sd_form
  population "the Table 6 standard deviation divides by the number of periods"
  sample "the Table 6 standard deviation divides by the number of periods less one"

axis stat_round
  down "Table 6 statistics truncated to 0.1%"
  half-even "Table 6 statistics to the nearest 0.1%, ties to even"
  half-up "Table 6 statistics to the nearest 0.1%, ties up"

axis zero_end
  fails "a terminal value of exactly $0 fails: abstract 'greater than zero', methodology 'positive'"
  succeeds "a terminal value of exactly $0 succeeds: introduction 'zero or greater'"

index asset_cls = [stocks, bonds, bills]

index cyr = year 1925..1996

index era = [e1926, e1946]

index hz = [y15, y20, y25, y30]

index mix = [s100, s75, s50, s25, s0, m603010]

index mon = month 1926-01..1997-12

index range_end = [low, high]
  note "the two ends of the abstract's range of withdrawal rates"

index step = int 0..48

index wd = [fixed, indexed]

index wr = [r03, r04, r05, r06, r07, r08, r09, r10, r11, r12]

input abstract_era[b in range_end]: key era question "Which period does this end of the abstract's range read, 1926-1997 or 1946-1997? The abstract names none"

input abstract_hz[b in range_end]: key hz question "Which payout period gives this end of the abstract's range? The abstract names none"

input abstract_level[b in range_end]: num question "Which success rate must every cell reach for this end of the abstract's range? The abstract names none"

input alloc[x in mix, a in asset_cls]: num

input annual_offset: int

input annual_start_12: int
  note "lifted from an inline figure of tally 1.0.1"

input cpi_avg[y in cyr]: num question "Annual average CPI-U for this year (Ibbotson SBBI 1998): the case holds no CPI data"

input cpi_base_year: key cyr

input cpi_dec[y in cyr]: num question "December CPI-U for this year (Ibbotson SBBI 1998): the case holds no CPI data"

input data_end: key mon

input dev2_2: int
  note "lifted from an inline figure of tally 1.0.1"

input era_from[r in era]: key mon

input hz_years[h in hz]: int

input min_stock_25: num

input min_stock_50: num

input min_stock_75: num

input monthly_start_12: int
  note "lifted from an inline figure of tally 1.0.1"

input need_12: int
  note "lifted from an inline figure of tally 1.0.1"

input rate0_0_000000000001: num
  note "lifted from an inline figure of tally 1.0.1"

input rate0_12: int
  note "lifted from an inline figure of tally 1.0.1"

input ret[a in asset_cls, m in mon]: num question "Total return of this asset class for this month, Ibbotson SBBI 1998: S&P 500; the corporate bond return 'calculated from' the Salomon Brothers Long-Term High-Grade Corporate Bond Index and S&P monthly high-grade corporate yields (splice dates and formula not stated); 30-day Treasury bills (compounding not stated). Commercial data, not in the case"

input success_target: num

input t6_median_2: int
  note "lifted from an inline figure of tally 1.0.1"

input tv_12: int
  note "lifted from an inline figure of tally 1.0.1"

input v0: num USD

input wrate[w in wr]: num

def abstract_rate[b in range_end]: num at reader
  note "an end of the abstract's range, read the way Results (PDF p. 4) reads the tables: the highest inflation-adjusted rate at which every stock/bond mix with at least 75% stock reaches the success level, for the abstract's period and payout period, which it doesn't name"
  rule base = wrate[last(w in wr where all(rate_pct[abstract_era[b], x, abstract_hz[b], w, indexed] >= abstract_level[b] for x in mix where alloc[x, bills] == 0 and alloc[x, stocks] >= min_stock_75))]

def annual_start[r in era, h in hz, c in mon]: bool at start_of(c)
  note "Tables 1-5 use 'annual overlapping periods': one start every 12 months, from era_from[r] moved by annual_offset months. The article does not name the month (case: Missing facts, first bullet); the offset is an assumed row"
  rule base = monthly_start[r, h, c] and c >= era_from[r] + annual_offset and (c - era_from[r] - annual_offset) / annual_start_12 == round((c - era_from[r] - annual_offset) / annual_start_12, 1, down)

def cpi_used[y in cyr]: num at start_of(y)
  rule avg beats base = cpi_avg[y] when cpi_value == annual_avg
  rule base = cpi_dec[y]

def dev2[r in era, h in hz, d in wd, c in mon]: num = pow(rate0[c, m603010, h, d] - t6_mean[r, h, d], dev2_2) at start_of(c)

def disc[c in mon, x in mix, k in step]: num at start_of(c)
  note "1 / the growth of $1 from the start of month c to the end of month c + k - 1 (1 at k = 0). No source rounds, so nothing is rounded here; at 360 steps of returns with a few decimals the exact value stays under the 4 096-digit cap"
  rule init = 1 when k == 0
  rule next = disc[c, x, k - 1] / (1 + port_r[x, c + k - 1]) when k > 0

def monthly_start[r in era, h in hz, c in mon]: bool = c >= era_from[r] and pos(c) + monthly_start_12 * hz_years[h] - 1 <= pos(data_end) at start_of(c)

def n_annual[r in era, h in hz]: int = count(c in mon where annual_start[r, h, c]) at reader

def n_monthly[r in era, h in hz]: int = count(c in mon where monthly_start[r, h, c]) at reader

def need[c in mon, x in mix, h in hz, d in wd]: num = sum(wscale[c, d, c + k - 1] * disc[c, x, k] for k in step where k >= 1 and k <= need_12 * hz_years[h]) at start_of(c)

def port_r[x in mix, m in mon]: num = sum(alloc[x, a] * ret[a, m] for a in asset_cls where alloc[x, a] > 0) at start_of(m)

def rate0[c in mon, x in mix, h in hz, d in wd]: num at start_of(c)
  note "Table 6: the annualized withdrawal rate that leaves exactly $0 at the end of the period. From V_T = 0, rate = 12 / need. The 1e-12 rounding is the modeller's, forced by the 4 096-digit cap (§7.1): no source rounds, and the Table 6 sums over hundreds of exact monthly-cohort rates pass the cap"
  rule base = round(rate0_12 / need[c, x, h, d], rate0_0_000000000001, half-even)

def rate_pct[r in era, x in mix, h in hz, w in wr, d in wd]: num = round(rate_share[r, x, h, w, d] / 1 %, 1, pct_round) at reader

def rate_share[r in era, x in mix, h in hz, w in wr, d in wd]: num = share(success[c, x, h, w, d] for c in mon where annual_start[r, h, c]) at reader

def success[c in mon, x in mix, h in hz, w in wr, d in wd]: bool at start_of(c)
  rule base = tv[c, x, h, w, d] > 0
  rule zero_ok beats base = tv[c, x, h, w, d] >= 0 when zero_end == succeeds

def t6_max[r in era, h in hz, d in wd]: num = max(rate0[c, m603010, h, d] for c in mon where monthly_start[r, h, c]) at reader

def t6_mean[r in era, h in hz, d in wd]: num = mean(rate0[c, m603010, h, d] for c in mon where monthly_start[r, h, c]) at reader

def t6_median[r in era, h in hz, d in wd]: num at reader
  note "Table 6 'Median': the type 1 quantile at 1/2 of the monthly cohorts' rate0, which is the middle cohort, since every column has an odd number of monthly starts"
  rule base = quantile(rate0[c, m603010, h, d] for c in mon where monthly_start[r, h, c], 1 / t6_median_2)

def t6_min[r in era, h in hz, d in wd]: num = min(rate0[c, m603010, h, d] for c in mon where monthly_start[r, h, c]) at reader

def t6_sd[r in era, h in hz, d in wd]: num at reader
  note "The 1e-12 precision of the square root is the modeller's; the table prints 0.1%"
  rule base = sqrt(t6_ss[r, h, d] / n_monthly[r, h]) to 1e-12
  rule sample beats base = sqrt(t6_ss[r, h, d] / (n_monthly[r, h] - 1)) to 1e-12 when sd_form == sample

def t6_ss[r in era, h in hz, d in wd]: num = sum(dev2[r, h, d, c] for c in mon where monthly_start[r, h, c]) at reader

def tv[c in mon, x in mix, h in hz, w in wr, d in wd]: num USD at start_of(c)
  note "The terminal value per v0 of Equation (1) (fixed) or (2) (indexed), in closed form"
  rule base = v0 * (1 - wrate[w] / tv_12 * need[c, x, h, d]) / disc[c, x, tv_12 * hz_years[h]]

def wscale[c in mon, d in wd, m in mon]: num at start_of(c)
  note "Equation (2): Wt x CPI(Y-1) / CPI(1925), where Y is the year of month t ('with a one-year lag'). Fixed withdrawals (Equation 1) are not scaled"
  rule fixed = 1 when d == fixed
  rule rebased = cpi_used[year_of(m) - 1] / cpi_used[year_of(c) - 1] when d == indexed and cpi_base == rebased
  rule y1925 = cpi_used[year_of(m) - 1] / cpi_used[cpi_base_year] when d == indexed and cpi_base == y1925

ask abstract_range: abstract_rate[b] for b in range_end with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, pct_round = half-up, zero_end = fails law 2026-10-18

ask ex_t1_min50: wrate[last(w in wr where all(rate_pct[e1926, x, y20, w, fixed] >= success_target for x in mix where alloc[x, bills] == 0 and alloc[x, stocks] >= min_stock_50))] with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, pct_round = half-up, zero_end = fails law 2026-10-18

ask ex_t2_min50: wrate[last(w in wr where all(rate_pct[e1926, x, y20, w, indexed] >= success_target for x in mix where alloc[x, bills] == 0 and alloc[x, stocks] >= min_stock_50))] with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, pct_round = half-up, zero_end = fails law 2026-10-18

ask ex_t3_min50: wrate[last(w in wr where all(rate_pct[e1946, x, y20, w, fixed] >= success_target for x in mix where alloc[x, bills] == 0 and alloc[x, stocks] >= min_stock_50))] with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, pct_round = half-up, zero_end = fails law 2026-10-18

ask ex_t3_s100: wrate[last(w in wr where rate_pct[e1946, s100, y20, w, fixed] >= success_target)] with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, pct_round = half-up, zero_end = fails law 2026-10-18

ask ex_t4_min25: wrate[last(w in wr where all(rate_pct[e1946, x, y20, w, indexed] >= success_target for x in mix where alloc[x, bills] == 0 and alloc[x, stocks] >= min_stock_25))] with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, pct_round = half-up, zero_end = fails law 2026-10-18

ask ex_t4_s100_r06: rate_pct[e1946, s100, y20, r06, indexed] with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, pct_round = half-up, zero_end = fails law 2026-10-18

ask instances: count(r in era, x in mix, d in wd, w in wr where rate_pct[r, x, y30, w, d] > rate_pct[r, x, y25, w, d]) with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, pct_round = half-up, zero_end = fails law 2026-10-18

ask periods_1926: n_annual[e1926, h] for h in hz law 2026-10-18

ask periods_1946: n_annual[e1946, h] for h in hz law 2026-10-18

ask t1_s100_y20: rate_pct[e1926, s100, y20, w, fixed] for w in wr with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, pct_round = half-up, zero_end = fails law 2026-10-18

ask t2_s100_y20: rate_pct[e1926, s100, y20, w, indexed] for w in wr with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, pct_round = half-up, zero_end = fails law 2026-10-18

ask t3_s0_y30: rate_pct[e1946, s0, y30, w, fixed] for w in wr with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, pct_round = half-up, zero_end = fails law 2026-10-18

ask t4_s50_y25: rate_pct[e1946, s50, y25, w, indexed] for w in wr with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, pct_round = half-up, zero_end = fails law 2026-10-18

ask t5_e1926_fixed_y20: rate_pct[e1926, m603010, y20, w, fixed] for w in wr with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, pct_round = half-up, zero_end = fails law 2026-10-18

ask t5_e1946_indexed_y30: rate_pct[e1946, m603010, y30, w, indexed] for w in wr with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, pct_round = half-up, zero_end = fails law 2026-10-18

ask t6_text: round(t6_mean[e1946, y20, indexed] / 1 %, 0.1, stat_round), round(t6_median[e1946, y20, indexed] / 1 %, 0.1, stat_round), round(t6_min[e1946, y20, indexed] / 1 %, 0.1, stat_round) with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, stat_round = half-up law 2026-10-18

ask t6a_max: round(t6_max[r, h, fixed] / 1 %, 0.1, stat_round) for r in era, h in hz with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, stat_round = half-up law 2026-10-18

ask t6a_mean: round(t6_mean[r, h, fixed] / 1 %, 0.1, stat_round) for r in era, h in hz with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, stat_round = half-up law 2026-10-18

ask t6a_median: round(t6_median[r, h, fixed] / 1 %, 0.1, stat_round) for r in era, h in hz with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, stat_round = half-up law 2026-10-18

ask t6a_min: round(t6_min[r, h, fixed] / 1 %, 0.1, stat_round) for r in era, h in hz with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, stat_round = half-up law 2026-10-18

ask t6a_sd: round(t6_sd[r, h, fixed] / 1 %, 0.1, stat_round) for r in era, h in hz with cpi_base = y1925, cpi_value = december, sd_form = population, stat_round = half-up law 2026-10-18

version lifted_figures
  cite lifted_1_0_1
  governs always
  known 1999-12-31
  annual_start_12 = 12 "inline in tally 1.0.1: annual_start line 100, factor"
  dev2_2 = 2 "inline in tally 1.0.1: dev2 line 106, argument 2 of pow"
  monthly_start_12 = 12 "inline in tally 1.0.1: monthly_start line 113, factor"
  need_12 = 12 "inline in tally 1.0.1: need line 119, factor"
  rate0_0_000000000001 = 0.000000000001 "inline in tally 1.0.1: rate0 line 125, round step"
  rate0_12 = 12 "inline in tally 1.0.1: rate0 line 125, factor"
  t6_median_2 = 2 "inline in tally 1.0.1: t6_median line 141, factor"
  tv_12 = 12 "inline in tally 1.0.1: tv line 154, factor"

version trinity99_v
  cite trinity99
  governs always
  known 1999-12-31
  note "known: the article is dated only by its volume and year, Financial Counseling and Planning 10(1), 1999, and every page footer reads '©1999'; web searches found no month or day of issue. Of the precise stamp of the form read (the mirror PDF's creation, 2006-05-01), the year's last day and the retrieval day (2026-10-18), §4.5 takes the earliest, the year's last day. Round 2 took the retrieval day. The assumed annual_offset row stands for a fact the article leaves out, so it is known from the model's on and sits in trinity99_ex_v (§4.5)"
  alloc[s100, stocks] = 1 "Tables 1-4 rows: 100% Stocks"
  alloc[s100, bonds] = 0 "Tables 1-4 rows: 100% Stocks"
  alloc[s100, bills] = 0 "Tables 1-4 rows: 100% Stocks"
  alloc[s75, stocks] = 0.75 "Tables 1-4 rows: 75% Stocks/25% Bonds"
  alloc[s75, bonds] = 0.25 "Tables 1-4 rows: 75% Stocks/25% Bonds"
  alloc[s75, bills] = 0 "Tables 1-4 rows: 75% Stocks/25% Bonds"
  alloc[s50, stocks] = 0.5 "Tables 1-4 rows: 50% Stocks/50% Bonds"
  alloc[s50, bonds] = 0.5 "Tables 1-4 rows: 50% Stocks/50% Bonds"
  alloc[s50, bills] = 0 "Tables 1-4 rows: 50% Stocks/50% Bonds"
  alloc[s25, stocks] = 0.25 "Tables 1-4 rows: 25% Stocks/75% Bonds"
  alloc[s25, bonds] = 0.75 "Tables 1-4 rows: 25% Stocks/75% Bonds"
  alloc[s25, bills] = 0 "Tables 1-4 rows: 25% Stocks/75% Bonds"
  alloc[s0, stocks] = 0 "Tables 1-4 rows: 100% Bonds"
  alloc[s0, bonds] = 1 "Tables 1-4 rows: 100% Bonds"
  alloc[s0, bills] = 0 "Tables 1-4 rows: 100% Bonds"
  alloc[m603010, stocks] = 0.6 "Tables 5 and 6 titles: 60% Stock, 30% Bonds, and 10% Treasury Bills"
  alloc[m603010, bonds] = 0.3 "Tables 5 and 6 titles: 60% Stock, 30% Bonds, and 10% Treasury Bills"
  alloc[m603010, bills] = 0.1 "Tables 5 and 6 titles: 60% Stock, 30% Bonds, and 10% Treasury Bills"
  cpi_base_year = 1925 "Methodology, PDF p. 3, Equation (2): Vt = Vt-1(1 + Rt) - Wt(CPIY-1/CPI1925)"
  data_end = 1997-12 "Methodology, PDF p. 3: overlapping periods from January 1926 through December 1997"
  era_from[e1926] = 1926-01 "Methodology, PDF p. 3: from January 1926; Tables 1, 2 and 5 (upper block): 1926 to 1997"
  era_from[e1946] = 1946-01 "Tables 3, 4 and 5 (lower block): 1946 to 1997; PDF p. 8: January 1946 through December 1997"
  min_stock_25 = 0.25 "Results, PDF p. 4: 'a portfolio of at least 25% stock'"
  min_stock_50 = 0.5 "Results, PDF p. 4: 'at least 50% stock'"
  min_stock_75 = 0.75 "Abstract, PDF p. 1: portfolios of at least 75% stock"
  success_target = 75 "Results, PDF p. 4: the worked readings of Tables 1-4 at a 75% success rate for a 20-year payout"
  v0 = 1000 "Methodology, PDF p. 3: 'the value per $1,000'"
  wrate[r03] = 0.03 "PDF p. 4: '0.25% per month (3% annualized)'; table headers: 3%"
  wrate[r04] = 0.04 "table headers: 4%"
  wrate[r05] = 0.05 "table headers: 5%"
  wrate[r06] = 0.06 "table headers: 6%"
  wrate[r07] = 0.07 "table headers: 7%"
  wrate[r08] = 0.08 "table headers: 8%"
  wrate[r09] = 0.09 "table headers: 9%"
  wrate[r10] = 0.1 "table headers: 10%"
  wrate[r11] = 0.11 "table headers: 11%"
  wrate[r12] = 0.12 "PDF p. 4: '1.0% per month (12% annualized)'; table headers: 12%"

version light_sizes
  cite light_cut
  governs always
  known 2026-10-18
  note "known: the model's on. The payout periods are the cut-down's size, chosen so that the reference interpreter runs it in minutes; LH-16's own rows (trinity99_v: 15, 20, 25 and 30 years, Methodology, PDF p. 3) are not in this file. The period counts follow from them (LH-16-light.md, part b); every other ask prints a hole"
  hz_years[y15] = 1 "light cut: stands for the 15-year period"
  hz_years[y20] = 2 "light cut: stands for the 20-year period"
  hz_years[y25] = 3 "light cut: stands for the 25-year period"
  hz_years[y30] = 4 "light cut: stands for the 30-year period"

version trinity99_ex_v
  cite trinity99
  governs always
  known 2026-10-18
  note "known: the model's on. The row is the modeller's stand-in for a fact of the article's own design that it leaves out (case: Missing facts, first bullet), so it takes the date of the case's stipulations (§4.5). Round 2 kept it in trinity99_v, when both were known on the same day"
  annual_offset = 0 assumed "the article names no start month for its annual periods; read as the month era_from names, January, the reading under which the methodology's period counts hold" "Methodology, PDF p. 3: 'annual overlapping periods'"
